  "chapter": 828,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 166 Chapter 828\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 3762, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  public health law, in relation to pharmacy\n        benefit managers; to amend the insurance  law,  in  relation  to\n        registration  and licensing of pharmacy benefit managers; and to\n        repeal certain provisions of  the  public  health  law  relating\n        thereto\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill provides for licensure and registration of pharmacy benefit\nmanagers (PBMs), bringing these entities  under  the  purview  of  state\nregulators at the Department of Financial Services (DFS) and the Depart-\nment  of  Health  (DOH).  The  bill  requires  rigorous transparency and\ndisclosure requirements and outlines duties and  obligations  that  PBMs\nmust  adhere to when performing services for health plans and when deal-\ning with covered individuals, pharmacies, and other providers.\n \n  This landmark bill enshrines in statute  the  most  comprehensive  PBM\nregulatory  structure  in  the  country.  It  will  shine a light on the\nactions of these entities that have  outsized  influence  on  healthcare\ncosts and the costs of prescription drugs. The accountability, transpar-\nency, and standard of fairness imposed in this bill will result in bene-\nfits  to  consumers in reduced prescription drug costs and the increased\nability to make more informed decisions about their healthcare coverage.\n \n  I have come to an agreement with the Legislature  to  amend  the  bill\nnext session to remedy several concerns. First, the amendment will allow\na  payer  to  impose  standards on pharmacies to address what would have\nbeen a significant fiscal impact to the State. Changes will also be made\nto the bill to clarify definitions to avoid  confusion  and  ensure  the\nregulated  community  understands  the duties imposed under the bill. An\nagreement was also reached to clarify that DFS is the entity  that  will\nprotect  covered  individuals and pursue violations of the law, ensuring\nthat PBMs are adhering to the law and  the  standards  imposed  by  this\nbill.  On  the  basis  of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill\ninto law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
